{"id": "EUVD-2026-108838", "enisaUuid": "a49072b2-88f6-322d-bc76-97e227516dba", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nice: fix metadata_dst refcount handling on representor teardown\n\nice_eswitch_release_repr() uses metadata_dst_free() to release the\nrepresentor's metadata_dst.  metadata_dst_free() directly frees the\nunderlying memory without checking the dst_entry refcount.\n\nWhen ice_eswitch_port_start_xmit() processes a packet, it takes a\nreference via dst_hold() and attaches the metadata_dst to the skb.\nIf the representor is torn down while packets are still queued on\nthe lower device (e.g. in a qdisc), the metadata_dst is freed while\nreferences are still held.\n\nUse dst_release() instead, which correctly decrements the refcount\nand only frees the object when all references are dropped.  The dst\nsubsystem already handles metadata_dst cleanup in dst_destroy() when\nDST_METADATA is set.\n\nOther drivers sharing this pattern (nfp, airoha, bnxt) already use\ndst_release() for their metadata_dst lifecycle.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f263235651775f93c15d90c9f25c3f4a4ef6512", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f5544f53f1e58ea8a49fb9f9158d5793b9205b0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/beb05f484a1e4a5a66e3678e4b7f3147f651c080", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e4d20db5179e83a4948927bc39e489a9a83256d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/58858b8f14803a7eeac297b3ce20f3b21bf2ff66"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99043"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b04b103-c3e0-3222-b0ee-70b56e81b48f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "18873fea-c189-3e7c-970d-294b1e536ff6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.16"}, {"id": "53a7f2b3-8182-3651-8ddd-052124bf1145", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5396b8a663f7a78ee5b75a47ee524b40795b265 <1f263235651775f93c15d90c9f25c3f4a4ef6512"}, {"id": "6a6b1c51-2784-314e-87b0-5bbb0b0ed880", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5396b8a663f7a78ee5b75a47ee524b40795b265 <5e4d20db5179e83a4948927bc39e489a9a83256d"}, {"id": "6cd39841-80e0-3cdd-8d50-22b3582b0900", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5396b8a663f7a78ee5b75a47ee524b40795b265 <6f5544f53f1e58ea8a49fb9f9158d5793b9205b0"}, {"id": "9a847829-0b39-3cad-8f9e-30d334252e49", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "bbf14ed7-8f3e-3520-98fb-d8e280c23d14", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "c05fbee9-8638-32cd-8867-d71f5f7c8372", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "d3b57927-591b-3fc4-884e-e46fa7d880c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5396b8a663f7a78ee5b75a47ee524b40795b265 <58858b8f14803a7eeac297b3ce20f3b21bf2ff66"}, {"id": "ed35a8f4-a0bd-36ad-8758-5a75225d3373", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "eff4359f-a233-3b5f-bfcf-2876c122fa08", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f5396b8a663f7a78ee5b75a47ee524b40795b265 <beb05f484a1e4a5a66e3678e4b7f3147f651c080"}, {"id": "fd9f98a8-585b-3200-8eb9-39faa6cd37c6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "6939d96d-05ad-333a-ba7f-b35095ba14ed", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}